WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.427
Why should a big country

2
00:00:01.427 --> 00:00:02.901
give more than it takes?

3
00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.602
That was the idea behind

4
00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:06.485
the Gujral Doctrine.

5
00:00:06.832 --> 00:00:08.159
I. K.

6
00:00:08.159 --> 00:00:09.838
Gujral set it out in

7
00:00:09.838 --> 00:00:12.286
1996, as foreign minister.

8
00:00:12.286 --> 00:00:13.985
He became prime minister the

9
00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:15.155
next year.

10
00:00:15.479 --> 00:00:17.503
India would not demand reciprocity

11
00:00:17.503 --> 00:00:19.219
from smaller neighbours.

12
00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.561
Plus non-interference,

13
00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:23.227
and peaceful settlement of disputes.

14
00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:25.572
Foreign policy rests on geography

15
00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:26.763
and history,

16
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:28.679
and on domestic politics and

17
00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:30.028
the economy.

18
00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:31.540
Your turn.

19
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.705
What was the key principle?
